# Python bytecode -- regenerated on every run
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Claude Code session history (recall plugin)
.recall/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Run outputs under projects/
#
# projects/sorghum-plastidial/ is the published snapshot and IS tracked: a
# thinned subset of checkpoints, enough to reproduce the paper's numbers. Those
# files are already tracked, and git never ignores a tracked file, so the broad
# patterns below only hide the untracked remainder -- the full checkpoint series
# kept locally so the figures can be regenerated.
#
# Everything for Poplar is local only. The manuscript figures need both species,
# but only Sorghum is published; the full sweep is deposited separately.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
projects/poplar-plastidial/
projects/qpsi-260406-plastid-*/
projects/*.tar.gz

# The un-thinned checkpoint series, and the derived matrices dropped from the
# snapshot because they are recomputable from the model.
projects/*/ml/*/checkpoints/V_step_*.tsv
projects/*/ml/*/checkpoints/Losses_step_*.tsv
projects/*/ml/*/results/*_Pout.tsv
projects/*/ml/*/finalize/
projects/*/ml/*/initialize/
projects/*/ml/training/temp_Pout.tsv

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Figure inputs that are not ours to publish.
#
# analysis_cache/ holds the cross-species TSVs the figure scripts read. They
# are derived from both species and the Poplar half is not distributed here,
# so they stay local -- on this machine it is a symlink to the working copy.
# analysis_cache/ is overridable with BIOFLUX_CROSS_DIR.
#
# data/ is tracked in full: the GLK gene-tree evidence and the measured
# phenotype data are both part of the published record.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Paper_Figures/analysis_cache

# fig_bio_rslt.py writes one PNG per penalty; only the un-suffixed copy at the
# operating point is the manuscript figure and is tracked.
Paper_Figures/fig_bio_rslt_p*.png
